cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite P-System if you use this software in your research."
title: "P-System: a registry of single-owner state with quorum certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amodio"
    given-names: "Paolo"
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "1.0.0"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaoloAmodio001/P-System"
abstract: >-
  A registry of single-owner state without global consensus: a committee of
  3f+1 validators decides, for each sender and nonce, which version runs,
  with rounds that end a split vote under partial synchrony, and every node
  derives the same state from the same set of decided events. Python
  implementation whose vote lock, execution and rounds are compiled Lean 4
  definitions, with machine-checked theorems about safety, progress and the
  boundary between Python and Lean.
keywords:
  - distributed systems
  - quorum certificates
  - Byzantine fault model
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
